# Sample circuit (PARTS.md "Done when"): 1 MHz oscillator, 8-bit counter from two
# cascaded 74LS161, a 74LS74 toggle that divides C7 by two, and a NAND decode of C6, C7.

part X1 OSC freq=1MHz
part J1 POWER
part R1 R value=4k7
part U1 74LS161
part U2 74LS161
part U3 74LS74
part U4 74LS00

net CLK      X1.OUT U1.CLK U2.CLK
net RESET_N  R1.2 U1.CLR_N U2.CLR_N
net VCC      R1.1

# Counter: U1 low nibble, U2 high nibble, enabled by U1's ripple carry.
net VCC      U1.ENP U1.ENT U1.LOAD_N U2.ENP U2.LOAD_N
net GND      U1.A U1.B U1.C U1.D U2.A U2.B U2.C U2.D
net C0       U1.QA
net C1       U1.QB
net C2       U1.QC
net C3       U1.QD
net CARRY    U1.RCO U2.ENT
net C4       U2.QA
net C5       U2.QB
net C6       U2.QC U4.1A
net C7       U2.QD U3.1CLK U4.1B

# Divider: flip-flop 1 toggles on each rising C7; flip-flop 2 unused.
net DIV      U3.1Q
net DIV_N    U3.1Q_N U3.1D
net VCC      U3.1PRE_N U3.1CLR_N U3.2PRE_N U3.2CLR_N
net GND      U3.2CLK U3.2D

# Decode: TOP_N low when C6 and C7 are high; gates 2-4 unused.
net TOP_N    U4.1Y
net GND      U4.2A U4.2B U4.3A U4.3B U4.4A U4.4B
